  "nameStory": "",
  "description": "The Bar-winged Skimmer is a medium-sized dragonfly (not a plant) belonging to the Skimmer family (Libellulidae), characterized by distinctive dark markings on its wings. This species is commonly found throughout New England during the summer months, inhabiting freshwater environments.",
  "idTips": [
    {
      "label": "Wing Markings",
      "description": "Dark brown or black bands across the wings, particularly visible on the outer portions",
      "isPrimary": true
    },
    {
      "label": "Body Color",
      "description": "Males display a whitish or pale blue pruinescence on the abdomen, while females appear more amber or brown",
      "isPrimary": false
    },
    {
      "label": "Size",
      "description": "Medium-sized dragonfly with a wingspan of approximately 2.5 to 3 inches",
      "isPrimary": false
    }
  ],
  "habitat": "Bar-winged Skimmers prefer ponds, lakes, and slow-moving streams with emergent vegetation and clear water.",
  "seasonality": {
    "spring": "",
    "summer": "",
    "fall": "",
    "winter": ""
  },
  "funFact": "Male Bar-winged Skimmers are highly territorial and can often be seen perching conspicuously on vegetation or floating objects, darting out to chase away rivals and catch small flying insects mid-flight.",
